{"availability":"available","full":"SandeepBaskaran/design-mode","name":"design-mode","description":"A visual editor for the browser to communicate with your coding agent.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":54,"forks":12,"created":"2026-04-27T04:08:30Z","updated":"2026-10-03T16:08:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://designmode.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://designmode.app/demo","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:23.554Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:23.554Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:16:23.554Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:32:57.287Z","stars":53,"forks":12},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:23.554Z","stars":54,"forks":12}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Design directly in your browser. Your agent writes the code.","A free, open-source browser extension (Chrome + Firefox) that turns any website into a live design surface. Edit layout, type, colour, spacing and structure with visual controls — then ship the result straight to Claude Code, Cursor, or any AI coding agent over MCP. No mock files, no copy-paste.","Design Mode is a visual editor that lives in your browser. Instead of describing UI changes in chat (\"make the button rounder, add more spacing, change the blue\"), you just drag, click, and type on the live site — and your AI coding agent reads those edits as a real diff. It works on any URL already in your tab: localhost, staging, or production. No Storybook, no mock files, no copy-paste."],"features":["Restyle any website without writing a single line of CSS.","Show your AI agent exactly what you want — visually — instead of describing it.","Drop sticky-note comments on elements and ship them with the prompt.","Export your changes as ready-to-paste CSS, Tailwind, SCSS, or JSX.","Opt-in anonymous analytics helps prioritize what actually gets built next."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SandeepBaskaran/design-mode/blob/main/README.md","fin